  (https://github.com/pymupdf/PyMuPDF). meal_log itself does not call PyMuPDF.
- basic_agent (MIT, https://github.com/Taeksu-Kim/basic_agent) — OpenAI-compatible client for the local LLM (optional).
- FastAPI, Starlette, Uvicorn, pydantic, python-multipart, httpx, requests (MIT / BSD / Apache-2.0) — the server.
- Pillow (MIT-CMU) — image normalization for uploaded captures.
- Optional: pytest (MIT), Playwright (Apache-2.0) for tests and the browser check; pandas, xlrd (BSD) for the kcal DB tools.
- Optional external services, run separately: the OCR server from doc_reader (PaddleOCR-VL, Apache-2.0), a local LLM server
  (vLLM, Apache-2.0) and Claude Code (Anthropic, under its own terms). Model weights are downloaded under their own licenses.

Nutrition reference values: kcal ranges in meal_log/menu_kcal.py and meal_log/compose.py are hand-written estimates or
values transcribed from the Korean MFDS "전국통합식품영양성분정보 음식 표준데이터" (public data, data.go.kr). The data file
itself is not included.
